2. Ridge risk (1/2n)||y - Xb||^2 + (lam/2)||b||^2
   lam =  0.0: mu =   0.9297, L =  99.8013, kappa = L/mu =    107.4
   lam =  0.1: mu =   1.0297, L =  99.9013, kappa = L/mu =     97.0
   lam =  1.0: mu =   1.9297, L = 100.8013, kappa = L/mu =     52.2
   after standardising: kappa = 1.19
3. Jensen check for f(x) = log(1 + exp(x)) on random pairs
   min of theta f(a) + (1-theta) f(b) - f(mix) = 1.05e-11
4. Cobb-Douglas u = x1^0.3 x2^0.5: concave? quasi-concave?
   Hessian eigenvalues at (2,3): [-0.1451 -0.0261] -> concave
   with a=0.9, c=0.8 (sum > 1): [-0.6299  0.4489] -> not concave
   but min u(mix) - min(u_a, u_b) = 1.23e-05 >= 0 -> quasi-concave
